00:01:31.622 --> 00:01:36.222
Yield curve steepness analysis is the bond filter I want sitting on your desk when a central

00:01:36.222 --> 00:01:37.782
bank decision is hours away.

00:01:38.362 --> 00:01:46.642
The two-year treasury yield stood at 4.7494%, while the 30 year reached 5.32%, a 57 basis

00:01:46.642 --> 00:01:50.482
point spread that says the market anticipates limited near-term easing.

00:01:50.482 --> 00:01:55.462
Think of that gap like the extra a contractor charges to finish a house on a 30-year clock

00:01:55.462 --> 00:01:56.822
instead of a 2-year one.

00:01:57.242 --> 00:02:02.362
57 basis points is a thin premium, which means nobody is paying you much to lock money

00:02:02.362 --> 00:02:03.082
up for decades.

00:02:03.682 --> 00:02:08.062
You open a brokerage bond screener, select investment grade corporates maturing between

00:02:08.062 --> 00:02:12.442
2028 and 2030, and compare each yield to that 2-year benchmark.

00:02:12.902 --> 00:02:17.282
You are hunting names that offer at least 80 basis points of extra carry over the short

00:02:17.282 --> 00:02:22.582
end, and you filter the same list for option-adjusted spreads so you can see how much extra the market

00:02:22.582 --> 00:02:27.822
demands for credit risk at each maturity. That screen draws on the forward curve inside the

00:02:27.822 --> 00:02:34.622
CME FedWatch tool, where a 76.5% chance of a 25 basis point hike by the December 9th meeting

00:02:34.622 --> 00:02:39.882
already prices modest further tightening. You see a five-year investment grade name showing 90

00:02:39.882 --> 00:02:45.522
basis points of carry over the two year. Do you extend duration for that extra coupon or stay short

00:02:45.522 --> 00:02:50.742
because the curve is still pricing a hike. Here is how I work it. I only extend if the extra

00:02:50.742 --> 00:02:56.362
carry clears 80 basis points and the option adjusted spread has not already blown out. If it has,

00:02:56.662 --> 00:03:01.562
the market has prepaid you for the risk and the trade is stale. The concrete step is a price

00:03:01.562 --> 00:03:07.002
alert on the 10 year over 2 year spread at 60 basis points, and you review intermediate corporate

00:03:07.002 --> 00:03:13.222
holdings only if that spread widens before the next FOMC statement. Prices move inverse to yields,

00:03:13.222 --> 00:03:18.562
so a steepening curve that lifts longer yields faster than shorter ones cuts the present value of

00:03:18.562 --> 00:03:24.922
distant cash flows on those 2028-2030 bonds. If the curve instead flatens because inflation data

00:03:24.922 --> 00:03:30.262
surprises higher, even a carefully selected carry trade can lose ground as the whole curve shifts

00:03:30.262 --> 00:03:37.176
up together. Toronto Dominion Bank listed as TD on the TSX is the simulated weekly hold,

00:03:37.556 --> 00:03:42.836
and this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money. The strategy is a valuation

00:03:42.836 --> 00:03:47.796
entry on a Canadian bank trading below consensus fair value, with stable U.S.

00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:52.836
operations contributing 35% to 40% of net income, and it uses yield curve

00:03:52.836 --> 00:03:57.516
steepness analysis in one clause, a defensive lender when that curve is pricing

00:03:57.516 --> 00:04:02.296
limited near-term easing. Catalyst is stable capital ratios and that U.S.

00:04:02.436 --> 00:04:06.136
retail bank contribution as defensive earning support ahead of the bank of

00:04:06.136 --> 00:04:10.836
Canada decision. Technical setup is price action relative to the 50-session

00:04:10.836 --> 00:04:16.416
average close. The entry open must sit above that average for the valuation factor to line up with

00:04:16.416 --> 00:04:22.196
measured entry data. In validation is a close below that 50-session average on volume above the

00:04:22.196 --> 00:04:28.116
20-session average inside the hold window. If that prints, the thesis is done, and that line is

00:04:28.116 --> 00:04:34.756
named before the simulated money is at risk. A 6% stop caps the loss at $60 on the $1,000

00:04:34.756 --> 00:04:40.396
dollar position if it triggers interday, with a target of 2-5% over 5 sessions if the

00:04:40.396 --> 00:04:43.316
valuation gap narrows on stable rate expectations.

00:04:44.076 --> 00:04:49.216
Confidence is medium, two factors aligned, the valuation discount plus sector defensive

00:04:49.216 --> 00:04:54.276
characteristics, and one uncertainty around the exact timing of any Canadian rate move.

00:04:55.248 --> 00:04:59.608
Medium confidence valuation entries have been producing negative matched window alpha

00:04:59.608 --> 00:05:04.588
when the index itself declines, and this pick still leans on that family as a live

00:05:04.588 --> 00:05:07.308
test rather than pretending the factor has been paying.

00:05:07.908 --> 00:05:12.448
The hold tests whether a name already showing relative strength to its 50 session average

00:05:12.448 --> 00:05:17.708
can deliver positive alpha when the backdrop is a central bank decision rather than sector

00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:22.988
rotation, and it enters at the next session's open under the published rules judged against

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:25.248
the NASDAQ over its own five sessions.

00:05:25.788 --> 00:05:28.208
General Motors finished its five session hold.

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:33.588
The earlier weekly hold that ran from the Tuesday open to the Monday close, we simulated

00:05:33.588 --> 00:05:41.948
buying GM at $77.22 at that Tuesday open and exited at $76.31 at the Monday close.

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:48.508
The position lost 1.18%, $11.78 on the $1,000 stake.

00:05:49.128 --> 00:05:56.968
The NASDAQ over those same sessions fell 0.62%, so matched window alpha was minus 0.56%.

00:05:56.968 --> 00:06:02.848
Stated confidence was medium, stated in validation was an earnings miss of more than 5% versus

00:06:02.848 --> 00:06:08.328
consensus or guidance cut on North American auto demand, and that invalidation never mattered.

00:06:08.808 --> 00:06:13.488
The 6% stop was not reached, and it stayed out of the way when the thesis was not broken.

00:06:14.148 --> 00:06:18.848
The medium grade fit the mix setup. The earnings catalyst never arrived, and the position

00:06:18.848 --> 00:06:24.348
simply tracked the broader market lower. So a valuation thesis built on sector rotation still

00:06:24.348 --> 00:06:29.208
produced negative matched window alpha, while the index declined over the identical window.

00:06:29.208 --> 00:06:34.328
This did not work, and next time I would not let an earning surprise label carry a hold

00:06:34.328 --> 00:06:36.868
when the report sits outside the five-session window.

