00:09:36.465 --> 00:09:36.565
8.

00:09:36.925 --> 00:09:41.705
Within 90 minutes, the Treasury yield rises 8 basis points, and your corporate spread

00:09:41.705 --> 00:09:48.725
widens to 135 basis points, cutting the price by roughly 0.7%, even though the policy rate

00:09:48.725 --> 00:09:49.825
itself did not move.

00:09:50.425 --> 00:09:54.225
Do you sit through the press conference, or do you cut when the option-adjusted spread

00:09:54.225 --> 00:09:56.465
has already widened 15 basis points?

00:09:57.045 --> 00:09:58.325
Here is how I think about it.

00:09:58.865 --> 00:10:03.865
Dealers widen credit spreads when they anticipate slower future cuts, because the present value

00:10:03.865 --> 00:10:08.745
of the issuer's cash flows falls, and the risk of refinancing at higher rates increases.

00:10:09.265 --> 00:10:13.685
The professional habit is to check the option-adjusted spread on that bond every time the

00:10:13.685 --> 00:10:18.865
Fedwatch probability of a December hike moves more than 10 percentage points. If the spread

00:10:18.865 --> 00:10:23.845
has already widened 15 basis points or more, you reduce size before the statement rather

00:10:23.845 --> 00:10:28.765
than after. The common misconception is that an unchanged policy rate means unchanged

00:10:28.765 --> 00:10:33.845
bond prices. The fix is to treat the forward curve and the credit spread reaction as the

00:10:33.845 --> 00:10:39.305
actual trade signal, not the headline decision. Any statement language that shifts the expected

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:43.605
path of the federal funds rate changes the discount rate on every corporate cash flow

00:10:43.605 --> 00:10:48.445
beyond the next meeting, and investors who watch only the spot rate miss the repricing

00:10:48.445 --> 00:10:52.865
in that 90 minute window when the curve and the credit spread matrix adjusts together.

00:10:53.405 --> 00:10:59.374
Remember, the headline rate is not the trade signal. The forward curve is. Open your brokerage

00:10:59.374 --> 00:11:04.714
platform, pull the two-year and 10-year treasury yields, calculate the spread, and set an

00:11:04.714 --> 00:11:10.054
alert for a 10 basis point widening, then recalculate the approximate price impact on a sample

00:11:10.054 --> 00:11:15.774
5-year corporate using the option-adjusted spread already on the screen. Before we wrap, watch

00:11:15.774 --> 00:11:20.574
how that 10-year over two-year spread trades after today's statement, because that is the filter

00:11:20.574 --> 00:11:26.034
for the next session's open. That's modern investing techniques for today. If you found this useful,

